#: ../../tools/esm_tools.rst:71 aa298c23d6614950be461aa7a9c84ad4
msgid "**Name**: ``ESM_generate_protein_sequence``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/esm_tools.rst:73 a1734b05acbd40bd8754eeba533f08ee
msgid ""
"**Description**: Generate or complete a protein sequence using ESM3, "
"EvolutionaryScale's generative protein language model. Provide a "
"prompt\\_sequence with '\\_' characters marking positions to generate "
"(masked positions), and ESM3 will fill them in via iterative masked "
"language modeling. Can generate entire sequences from scratch (all '\\_')"
" or complete partial sequences. Use for: protein engineering, de novo "
"protein design, completing truncated sequences, exploring sequence space "
"around a template. Prerequisites: pip install esm; set ESM\\_API\\_KEY "
"(from https://forge.evolutionaryscale.ai). Example: "
"'MKTAY\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_QRQIS' generates 5 residues in the masked region."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/esm_tools.rst:80 eefd135071fd4e6da42e7d1b046ed812
msgid ""
"``prompt_sequence`` (string) (required) Protein sequence template with "
"'\\_' at positions to generate. Use standard amino acid letters for fixed"
" positions and '\\_' for masked/generated positions. Example: "
"'MKTAY\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_QRQISFVK' generates 5 residues in the middle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/esm_tools.rst:83 47dc3be18c704d048668d922bc19b366
msgid "``model`` (string) (optional) ESM3 model to use for generation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/esm_tools.rst:86 661e46168e0e43979501e0ccead41beb
msgid ""
"``num_steps`` (integer) (optional) Number of iterative decoding steps "
"(default: 8). More steps = slower but potentially better quality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/esm_tools.rst:89 51a31777ee8b4afe92d880f077ed4944
msgid ""
"``temperature`` (number) (optional) Sampling temperature (default: 1.0). "
"Lower values (0.1-0.5) produce more conservative sequences; higher values"
" (1.0-2.0) more diverse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/esm_tools.rst:107 e9f1d05937e84861b3ebce8357f10495
msgid "**ESM_get_protein_embedding** (Type: ESMTool)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/esm_tools.rst:109 2988507fc4314d2eb3aeec313940c3cd
msgid ""
"Get protein sequence embeddings from EvolutionaryScale ESMC (ESM "
"Cambrian) models via the Forge A..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/esm_tools.rst 1fcb2780a5be43bea17ecdab572ba61c
msgid "ESM_get_protein_embedding tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/esm_tools.rst:115 c48127768082459b90663cef57c851f0
msgid "**Name**: ``ESM_get_protein_embedding``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/esm_tools.rst:117 ee9f10900aca43ba81e9e7e965ca34b9
msgid ""
"**Description**: Get protein sequence embeddings from EvolutionaryScale "
"ESMC (ESM Cambrian) models via the Forge API. Returns a mean-pooled "
"embedding vector (320-dim for esmc-300m, 1152-dim for esmc-600m) "
"representing the entire protein, and optionally per-residue embeddings. "
"ESMC is a fast, high-quality protein language model suitable for "
"downstream tasks: similarity search, clustering, property prediction. "
"Prerequisites: pip install esm; set ESM\\_API\\_KEY environment variable "
"(token from https://forge.evolutionaryscale.ai). Use for: encoding "
"protein sequences for ML, computing protein-protein similarity, "
"featurizing sequences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/esm_tools.rst:124 e280a1b8b6c94ada890d361902491f24
msgid ""
"``sequence`` (string) (required) Protein amino acid sequence in single-"
"letter code (e.g. 'MKTAYIAKQRQISFVKSHFSRQ'). Standard 20 amino acids; "
"avoid gaps or non-standard characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/esm_tools.rst:127 3016f7f2ed214eb9aa491eb99f3bdec3
msgid ""
"``model`` (string) (optional) ESMC model to use. 'esmc-300m-2024-12' "
"(faster, 300M params) or 'esmc-600m-2024-12' (more accurate, 600M "
"params)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/esm_tools.rst:130 8db9f593933e40509c4ea5ed0e4e8633
msgid ""
"``return_per_residue`` (boolean) (optional) If true, also return per-"
"residue embedding vectors (one vector per amino acid). Default false to "
"reduce response size."
msgstr ""

